WEBVTT

00:00:34.868 --> 00:00:36.870
Dateline Tarantulon 6.

00:00:36.954 --> 00:00:38.455
The brave warriors of Earth,

00:00:38.539 --> 00:00:42.084
under the command of General
Major Webelo Zapp Brannigan,

00:00:42.167 --> 00:00:44.962
have achieved victory
over the Spider homeworld.

00:00:49.341 --> 00:00:51.802
And to the victor belong the spoils.

00:00:51.885 --> 00:00:55.097
One trillion dollars in silken treasure.

00:00:56.098 --> 00:00:57.683
Mm.

00:00:57.933 --> 00:00:59.852
My fellow Earthicans,

00:00:59.935 --> 00:01:02.229
after meeting with top voodoo economists,

00:01:02.312 --> 00:01:06.733
I have decided to refund
our silk surplus to you, the taxpayers.

00:01:06.817 --> 00:01:10.654
That's right.
I've sent you each 300 buckaroos

00:01:10.737 --> 00:01:12.614
in the form of a Tricky Dick fun bill.

00:01:12.698 --> 00:01:14.658
Knock yourselves out.

00:01:16.952 --> 00:01:18.662
I'm slightly richer.

00:01:18.745 --> 00:01:20.497
What to do? What to do?

00:01:20.581 --> 00:01:24.376
One $300 hookerbot or 300 $1 hookerbots?

00:01:24.459 --> 00:01:26.044
I'm going to swim with a whale.

00:01:26.128 --> 00:01:28.130
They're the gentle giants of the deep.

00:01:28.213 --> 00:01:29.798
I'm well aware of that.

00:01:29.882 --> 00:01:33.635
Scruffy's going to get himself
one of them $300 haircuts.

00:01:33.719 --> 00:01:35.888
This one's lost its pizzazz.

00:01:36.555 --> 00:01:37.931
A fortune, it is.

00:01:38.015 --> 00:01:41.435
At last, Zoidberg
will live like a rich man.

00:01:43.228 --> 00:01:44.646
Go away. Get away from me.

00:01:44.980 --> 00:01:47.232
Shmeesh. It's just 300 bucks.

00:01:47.316 --> 00:01:49.234
What is that, like,
a hundred cups of coffee?

00:01:49.359 --> 00:01:50.402
That's it!

00:01:50.485 --> 00:01:53.113
I'm getting a hundred cups of coffee,
starting now.

00:01:54.031 --> 00:01:55.991
Coffee machine, one cup of coffee, please.

00:02:00.579 --> 00:02:01.705
Smells good.

00:02:05.417 --> 00:02:07.169
Leela, are you there?

00:02:07.252 --> 00:02:09.421
- No.
- Oh, yes, you are.

00:02:09.505 --> 00:02:12.090
I'm hereby inviting you
and your oddball coworkers

00:02:12.174 --> 00:02:16.303
to a special reception
to display the national silk surplus.

00:02:16.386 --> 00:02:19.973
I believe you know the heroic
space stallion who captured it.

00:02:20.057 --> 00:02:21.475
Show them my medal, Kif.

00:02:21.725 --> 00:02:24.561
He rented it with his tax refund.

00:02:24.645 --> 00:02:27.606
So, Leela, will you have the pleasure?

00:02:27.731 --> 00:02:29.816
What little there is to be had.

00:02:29.900 --> 00:02:31.318
Tomorrow night at 8:00, then.

00:02:31.401 --> 00:02:32.653
Smooches. Mwah.

00:02:39.535 --> 00:02:42.162
No cheap crack houses for me no more.

00:02:45.707 --> 00:02:46.792
Very good, sir.

00:02:46.875 --> 00:02:49.211
Shall I pre-warm sir's crack pipe?

00:02:55.676 --> 00:02:58.136
Oh, Kif, it was so romantic of you

00:02:58.220 --> 00:03:00.430
to rent this paddle plane
with your tax rebate.

00:03:00.514 --> 00:03:03.475
We're like two dandelion seeds
wafting on the breeze.

00:03:03.559 --> 00:03:06.812
Yes. Seeds. Wafting.

00:03:06.895 --> 00:03:09.439
I almost feel kind of shallow
for blowing my rebate

00:03:09.523 --> 00:03:11.316
on this cool talking tattoo.

00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:12.442
Hey, Gordon Gecko.

00:03:12.526 --> 00:03:14.695
I cost as much as this whole crummy date.

00:03:14.778 --> 00:03:16.029
Shut up!

00:03:16.113 --> 00:03:17.114
Ow!

00:03:20.742 --> 00:03:23.704
Ma'am, it has become too much of a chore

00:03:23.787 --> 00:03:26.248
for me to clean out my wrinkles each day.

00:03:26.331 --> 00:03:29.877
Is it true that stem cells
may fight the aging process?

00:03:29.960 --> 00:03:33.589
Well, yes, in the same way
an infant may fight Muhammad Ali, but...

00:03:33.672 --> 00:03:36.133
One pound of stem cells, please.

00:03:38.886 --> 00:03:43.265
Of course, any age-reversing effects
will be purely temporary...

00:03:51.857 --> 00:03:52.983
Oh.

00:03:53.442 --> 00:03:54.443
Ooh.

00:03:55.694 --> 00:03:57.654
Ooh-hoo-hoo.

00:04:00.365 --> 00:04:02.868
Oh! Oh-ho-ho-ho-ho.

00:04:02.951 --> 00:04:06.038
Say, buddy, why is
this Grand Cigar so pricey?

00:04:06.121 --> 00:04:07.831
Well, as you can see,

00:04:07.915 --> 00:04:11.460
its wrapper is a piece
of the original U.S. Constitution.

00:04:11.543 --> 00:04:15.881
It was hand-rolled by Queen Elizabeth
during her wild years

00:04:15.964 --> 00:04:20.511
and was buried with George Burns
until grave-robbing space mushrooms...

00:04:20.594 --> 00:04:21.887
Well, you know the rest.

00:04:21.970 --> 00:04:23.472
Give you 300 bucks for it.

00:04:23.555 --> 00:04:26.225
- No can do.
- Oh, all right.

00:04:26.308 --> 00:04:30.020
I'll just take these
$300 burglar's tools, then.

00:04:30.103 --> 00:04:31.271
Very good, sir.

00:04:32.439 --> 00:04:34.816
So, uh, what time you close tonight?

00:04:37.277 --> 00:04:39.279
Hey, Pops. Did that tax rebate come?

00:04:39.363 --> 00:04:40.906
Came and went.

00:04:40.989 --> 00:04:44.159
You're now the proud owner
of Bamboo Boogie Boots.

00:04:45.369 --> 00:04:48.288
With a warning label this big,
you know they got to be fun.

00:04:48.413 --> 00:04:50.457
But, Pops, I don't want to have fun.

00:04:50.541 --> 00:04:53.627
I want to be like you...
Boring, but prudently invested.

00:04:53.710 --> 00:04:55.212
Babylon's bells!

00:04:55.295 --> 00:04:58.632
I tallied almost 300 bananas
on this entertainment product.

00:04:58.715 --> 00:05:00.133
Now you put them on and have fun.

00:05:00.217 --> 00:05:01.468
I don't wanna!

00:05:01.552 --> 00:05:05.055
Well, then I'm gonna put them on
and make you watch me have fun.

00:05:05.138 --> 00:05:07.850
See? Fun, fun...

00:05:07.933 --> 00:05:10.060
Dwight! Help me!

00:05:10.143 --> 00:05:11.478
I'll save you, Pops.

00:05:23.407 --> 00:05:24.449
Hey!

00:05:24.533 --> 00:05:26.785
Turn that damn music...

00:05:27.369 --> 00:05:28.495
Up.

00:05:29.955 --> 00:05:31.164
Isn't this fun?

00:05:31.248 --> 00:05:34.168
No! I wish I had two mommies.

00:05:34.626 --> 00:05:36.920
Try these, uh, sir.

00:05:39.798 --> 00:05:43.135
I ask for rich guy stuff,
and you give me shiny pebbles?

00:05:43.218 --> 00:05:44.219
Bah!

00:05:44.303 --> 00:05:46.096
I bid you adieu.

00:05:48.182 --> 00:05:49.183
Ah!

00:05:57.357 --> 00:05:59.610
I'd like a pass
to swim with Mushu, please.

00:05:59.693 --> 00:06:01.403
Well, you asked the right guy.

00:06:01.486 --> 00:06:04.948
I'm the whale biologist.
Though, personally, I hate whales.

00:06:05.032 --> 00:06:06.241
Especially Mushu.

00:06:06.658 --> 00:06:08.410
Then why'd you become a whale biologist?

00:06:08.535 --> 00:06:10.746
I don't know you well enough
to get into that.

00:06:10.829 --> 00:06:11.997
$300 please.

00:06:13.874 --> 00:06:14.875
Noon tomorrow.

00:06:14.958 --> 00:06:17.127
If you're late, you only get to tread
water in the scallop tank.

00:06:21.048 --> 00:06:22.549
Yeah, I'll have a coffee.

00:06:22.633 --> 00:06:24.051
Guppy, trout, mermaid or...

00:06:24.134 --> 00:06:26.011
Whale, please.

00:06:33.852 --> 00:06:37.397
Amy, I... I also spent
some of my tax rebate

00:06:37.481 --> 00:06:39.942
on a gift for you.

00:06:40.817 --> 00:06:41.944
Oh, Kiffy.

00:06:43.195 --> 00:06:46.490
It shows the time
wherever we both are.

00:06:46.573 --> 00:06:48.617
And it's powered by love.

00:06:48.700 --> 00:06:50.369
Also, you have to wind it.

00:06:50.452 --> 00:06:53.664
Ooh! Somebody won big at skeeball.

00:06:53.747 --> 00:06:54.790
You shut up.

00:06:54.873 --> 00:06:56.041
I love it, Kif.

00:06:56.124 --> 00:06:58.293
I'll use it whenever I want
to know what time it is.

00:07:00.546 --> 00:07:01.964
Ooh, it's Fry and Leela.

00:07:02.339 --> 00:07:04.049
Hi, Fry and Leela!

00:07:04.132 --> 00:07:05.300
Ah!

00:07:05.384 --> 00:07:07.010
Ooh! Oh, my... Keep pedaling.

00:07:07.094 --> 00:07:08.595
Oh, for the love of God, keep pedaling.

00:07:16.353 --> 00:07:18.146
Phew.

00:07:18.564 --> 00:07:20.232
Bye, Fry and Leela!

00:07:23.110 --> 00:07:24.111
Oh.

00:07:30.325 --> 00:07:31.326
Oh!

00:07:31.410 --> 00:07:34.830
I can't wait till the tattoos
on Amy's butt hear about this.

00:07:34.913 --> 00:07:36.623
- Hear about what?
- Tell us!

00:07:43.922 --> 00:07:46.758
Don't feel sad, my little tadpole.

00:07:46.842 --> 00:07:50.095
I'm trying not to.

00:07:50.179 --> 00:07:53.307
But my gift to you
is in the belly of a whale.

00:07:53.390 --> 00:07:57.769
Say, this reminds me of that time
I ate that other watch Kif gave you.

00:07:57.853 --> 00:07:59.938
Hey, it is kind of like that.

00:08:00.022 --> 00:08:02.566
To induce vomiting, that was the solution.

00:08:02.649 --> 00:08:04.359
Everywhere, it went.

00:08:05.986 --> 00:08:08.405
What a Valentine's Day that was.

00:08:08.864 --> 00:08:09.865
Hmm.

00:08:09.948 --> 00:08:12.201
This may seem like a huge coincidence,

00:08:12.284 --> 00:08:14.411
but I happen to have
an "in" with that whale.

00:08:14.494 --> 00:08:16.330
Scruffy's formulated a plan.

00:08:16.413 --> 00:08:19.249
But you'll need a ready source
of nauseating rotten fish.

00:08:22.169 --> 00:08:23.629
Freshen your coffee, sir?

00:08:23.712 --> 00:08:25.214
Yeah, yeah, yeah. Keep it coming.

00:08:25.297 --> 00:08:26.465
Put the pot down. Get away!

00:08:31.803 --> 00:08:33.514
You're so young in spirit.

00:08:33.597 --> 00:08:36.558
It's hard to believe you're as old as 25.

00:08:36.642 --> 00:08:39.937
The key is to grab life by the ho-jos.

00:08:40.020 --> 00:08:42.689
Live every day like it might be your last.

00:08:43.190 --> 00:08:44.316
What'll it be, kids?

00:08:44.399 --> 00:08:46.985
One bowl of mild farina.

00:08:55.786 --> 00:08:56.828
Pay dirt.

00:08:57.454 --> 00:08:58.789
Hi-ya!

00:09:04.378 --> 00:09:05.879
Here you go, big spender.

00:09:05.963 --> 00:09:08.423
Foie gras and caviar.

00:09:10.050 --> 00:09:11.593
Goose liver?

00:09:11.802 --> 00:09:13.303
Fish eggs? Feh!

00:09:13.428 --> 00:09:15.722
Where's the goose? Where's the fish?

00:09:15.806 --> 00:09:19.226
Hey, that's what rich people eat,
the garbage parts of the food.

00:09:19.309 --> 00:09:23.272
I ate garbage yesterday
and it didn't cost me $300!

00:09:23.355 --> 00:09:24.690
I'm not paying!

00:09:24.773 --> 00:09:26.191
Farewell, good sir.

00:09:52.593 --> 00:09:55.053
The Grand Cigar, she is mine.

00:09:55.137 --> 00:09:58.182
And with absolutely no consequences.

00:10:15.115 --> 00:10:16.200
You see that?

00:10:16.283 --> 00:10:18.035
Grand theft tobacco.

00:10:18.118 --> 00:10:21.496
Time to get off
our fat cop asses and ride.

00:10:32.132 --> 00:10:33.342
Pee-ew!

00:10:33.425 --> 00:10:36.512
This fish is slightly too rotten
to even make jambalaya.

00:10:42.559 --> 00:10:43.852
So far, so good.

00:10:43.936 --> 00:10:45.020
Where's Kif?

00:10:53.695 --> 00:10:56.156
This isn't Yemeni, it's Sulawesi.

00:10:56.240 --> 00:10:58.492
And the cup's shaking.
I don't want my coffee shaking.

00:10:58.617 --> 00:11:01.912
You seem a tad wound up, buddy.
And your face is greasy.

00:11:01.995 --> 00:11:04.748
Real greasy. You been up all night?

00:11:04.831 --> 00:11:06.124
Of course I've been up all night!

00:11:06.208 --> 00:11:07.751
Not because of caffeine. It was insomnia.

00:11:07.835 --> 00:11:09.253
I couldn't stop thinking about coffee.

00:11:09.336 --> 00:11:10.921
I need a nap.

00:11:11.004 --> 00:11:12.005
Coffee time!

00:11:16.718 --> 00:11:18.428
Ah. Mighty fine smokable.

00:11:18.512 --> 00:11:20.722
Fancy cigar?
Why don't you smoke it already?

00:11:20.806 --> 00:11:22.474
Puff, puff. Go, go, go!

00:11:22.558 --> 00:11:25.644
Nah, you can't blow a smoke
from such a majestic stogie

00:11:25.727 --> 00:11:27.104
in just anyone's face.

00:11:27.187 --> 00:11:31.024
I'm saving it for the fancy pantses
at Zapp Brannigan's black-tie reception.

00:11:31.108 --> 00:11:32.109
You coming?

00:11:37.364 --> 00:11:40.576
And the fifth reason whales kill
is for the sheer fun of it.

00:11:40.659 --> 00:11:41.743
Anything else?

00:11:41.827 --> 00:11:43.912
Yeah, you're lumpy and you smell awful.

00:11:43.996 --> 00:11:46.081
Hey. I calls them like I sees them.

00:11:46.164 --> 00:11:47.457
I'm a whale biologist.

00:11:49.293 --> 00:11:52.796
Okay, Mushu, it's feeding time.

00:12:02.139 --> 00:12:04.850
Oh, crud, he ate my suit.

00:12:04.933 --> 00:12:06.226
The suit was ugly.

00:12:06.310 --> 00:12:07.436
Whale biologist.

00:12:15.903 --> 00:12:18.071
Perhaps if you tighten your grip, sir.

00:12:18.155 --> 00:12:20.490
Ah, thank you, golf slave.

00:12:22.284 --> 00:12:25.662
Bah! Rich people wouldn't waste
their time on this nonsense.

00:12:25.746 --> 00:12:27.831
Plus, these eggs are gritty and tasteless.

00:12:33.837 --> 00:12:36.089
Ow! Not so rough!

00:12:40.552 --> 00:12:44.223
Ladies and gentlemen, presenting Mushu,

00:12:44.306 --> 00:12:47.226
the educated whale
who thinks he's better than you.

00:12:49.102 --> 00:12:51.480
Come on, Mushu, barf!

00:12:51.563 --> 00:12:53.315
Barf like a freshman!

00:12:53.398 --> 00:12:57.110
And now, ignorant whale lovers,
we'll see who's boss

00:12:57.194 --> 00:12:59.321
as I make Mushu jump through this hoop.

00:12:59.404 --> 00:13:00.822
Jump, Mushu.

00:13:06.036 --> 00:13:07.621
Who wants a fish?

00:13:14.711 --> 00:13:16.547
Mushu is sad.

00:13:16.630 --> 00:13:19.424
It just keeps coming and coming.

00:13:22.886 --> 00:13:24.763
Wait, that chunk!

00:13:24.847 --> 00:13:26.098
It's the watch.

00:13:30.853 --> 00:13:33.146
I got it, Amy, I got it.

00:13:33.230 --> 00:13:34.606
The plan went off without a...

00:13:34.690 --> 00:13:36.942
He's got aquarium property! Stop him!

00:13:37.025 --> 00:13:38.652
Better do what he says.

00:13:38.735 --> 00:13:40.445
He's a whale biologist.

00:13:41.864 --> 00:13:43.740
You're under arrest, you squishy punk!

00:13:43.824 --> 00:13:45.909
Oh...

00:13:45.993 --> 00:13:47.327
Oh.

00:14:00.299 --> 00:14:04.094
The Spiderians, though weak
and womanlike on the battlefield,

00:14:04.178 --> 00:14:06.263
are masters of the textile arts.

00:14:06.346 --> 00:14:08.098
Taste like King Crab, by the way.

00:14:08.348 --> 00:14:12.853
Crazy bugs actually wove this tapestry
of my heroic conquest

00:14:12.936 --> 00:14:15.063
while I was still killing them.

00:14:18.025 --> 00:14:20.611
What? It's not even scratch-and-sniff?

00:14:20.694 --> 00:14:23.614
But if rich people think it's good,
I'll buy it.

00:14:23.697 --> 00:14:25.365
One art, please.

00:14:27.534 --> 00:14:31.163
What a clever impersonation
of a stupid poor person!

00:14:31.246 --> 00:14:33.874
How much is that place mat
actually worth, Brannigan?

00:14:33.957 --> 00:14:37.002
Exactly $1 billion.

00:14:37.586 --> 00:14:39.963
Now that's walkin' around money.

00:14:42.799 --> 00:14:44.718
What? Hey?

00:14:58.649 --> 00:15:00.067
So I said to Kitty,

00:15:00.150 --> 00:15:05.113
"The only way to keep the butler from
running away is to cut off his foot."

00:15:05.364 --> 00:15:06.615
Ah-ha-ha.

00:15:06.698 --> 00:15:07.950
Uh-huh.

00:15:08.033 --> 00:15:11.995
Yes, it reminds me of a joke I heard
about upper middle-class people.

00:15:15.666 --> 00:15:19.711
I've never been sad
at a party before.

00:15:19.795 --> 00:15:23.298
I wonder if my mind is thinking
about Kif being in jail.

00:15:23.423 --> 00:15:24.633
Jail's not so bad.

00:15:24.716 --> 00:15:26.760
You can make sangria in the toilet.

00:15:26.844 --> 00:15:28.804
Course, it's shank or be shanked.

00:15:28.887 --> 00:15:30.389
Of course.

00:15:32.558 --> 00:15:36.645
Look, just give back our property
and we'll drop the charges.

00:15:36.728 --> 00:15:38.438
Fine! Have the watch!

00:15:38.522 --> 00:15:39.606
It's broken anyway.

00:15:41.233 --> 00:15:42.442
I don't want your watch!

00:15:42.526 --> 00:15:44.778
You're covered in precious ambergris.

00:15:45.988 --> 00:15:47.447
Precious hamburgers?

00:15:50.075 --> 00:15:52.160
"Ambergris." Noun.

00:15:52.244 --> 00:15:55.622
A grease-like product
of the sperm whale's digestive tract

00:15:55.706 --> 00:15:58.625
that is used as a base
in the finest perfumes.

00:15:58.709 --> 00:16:02.504
This has been Roseanne,
your guide to the world of facts.

00:16:03.881 --> 00:16:05.090
You heard Roseanne.

00:16:05.174 --> 00:16:07.676
Scrape off the priceless ambergris
and I'll let you go.

00:16:07.759 --> 00:16:11.305
Or better yet, I'll simply shed my skin.

00:16:18.395 --> 00:16:20.230
Stop it. Stop it. It's fine!

00:16:20.314 --> 00:16:21.732
I will destroy you!

00:16:31.033 --> 00:16:32.201
Wha...

00:16:39.458 --> 00:16:41.001
Uh, got to go.

00:16:41.084 --> 00:16:42.294
Uh, fight club.

00:16:46.924 --> 00:16:48.884
What's happening, Hubie?

00:16:48.967 --> 00:16:51.803
Ah, I'm afraid the face
you fell in love with

00:16:51.887 --> 00:16:56.308
was actually just a blob of living gunk
I bought with my tax refund.

00:17:00.395 --> 00:17:03.398
Well, as long as we're being honest,

00:17:04.024 --> 00:17:08.195
I also spent my tax refund
on a crazy treatment.

00:17:10.280 --> 00:17:12.449
That certainly is honest.

00:17:12.783 --> 00:17:15.827
It's better for us to both
just be ourselves.

00:17:15.911 --> 00:17:18.247
You, wrinkled as a prune.

00:17:18.330 --> 00:17:20.958
You, fat as the queen of sea cows.

00:17:21.041 --> 00:17:22.876
I love you!

00:17:28.298 --> 00:17:32.135
So, you see, the putrid, waxy substance
I was coated with was...

00:17:32.219 --> 00:17:33.679
Not precious ambergris?

00:17:33.762 --> 00:17:37.766
Yes. And I managed to sneak some out
in the usual place.

00:17:38.141 --> 00:17:39.351
Ta-da!

00:17:39.852 --> 00:17:45.566
Using that, I'll make you a perfume
of lilac and jasmine and Franken Berry.

00:17:45.649 --> 00:17:47.985
Oh, Kif, it's so romantic.

00:17:48.068 --> 00:17:49.278
I can't even wait!

00:17:49.361 --> 00:17:50.904
I'm going to wear it right now.

00:17:52.155 --> 00:17:53.699
Bah!

00:17:57.327 --> 00:18:00.205
Who smells like freaking porpoise hork?

00:18:00.289 --> 00:18:02.332
I do. Kiss me, Kif.

00:18:10.174 --> 00:18:13.260
Oh, what a foolish squid I've been.

00:18:13.343 --> 00:18:14.469
I'm not rich.

00:18:14.553 --> 00:18:19.308
I can't even buy one measly masterpiece.

00:18:21.101 --> 00:18:22.394
Pardon us, gent.

00:18:22.477 --> 00:18:26.690
Might a couple of hungry, hungry hoboes
take a feed from that aluminum snack box?

00:18:29.359 --> 00:18:33.071
So now I'm in the gutter
surrounded by bums who eat garbage?

00:18:33.155 --> 00:18:35.574
Money brought me no happiness.

00:18:35.657 --> 00:18:36.700
Bubkes.

00:18:36.783 --> 00:18:39.203
Ooh, this boot's got
a little pudding at the bottom.

00:18:41.163 --> 00:18:44.625
Interestingly, the Spiderians
are more closely related

00:18:44.708 --> 00:18:47.169
to our elephants than our spiders.

00:18:53.800 --> 00:18:56.428
Don't mind us. Whoa, whoa!

00:19:11.360 --> 00:19:12.903
The loot! The loot!

00:19:12.986 --> 00:19:14.488
The loot is on fire!

00:19:15.489 --> 00:19:18.450
Leela, my precious rock dove,
I'll save you.

00:19:20.827 --> 00:19:22.955
Everyone, to the fire door!

00:19:23.038 --> 00:19:24.373
It's on fire!

00:19:25.624 --> 00:19:28.836
We're trapped, my sweet hippopotamus.

00:19:31.880 --> 00:19:34.633
Coffee, coffee, coffee!

00:20:32.024 --> 00:20:33.442
- Where are we, Pops?
- Wha...

00:20:33.525 --> 00:20:34.943
What happened to the food?

00:20:35.027 --> 00:20:38.113
I think we were saved
by a mysterious orange blur.

00:20:38.197 --> 00:20:40.324
Welcome, one and all.

00:20:40.824 --> 00:20:43.952
I finally figured out
how money could make me happy,

00:20:44.036 --> 00:20:46.914
by using it to buy
my hungry friends a feast!

00:20:48.749 --> 00:20:49.958
Everyone join us.

00:20:50.042 --> 00:20:53.962
Oysters Rockefeller here
has provided genuine turkey dogs!

00:20:54.338 --> 00:20:57.966
Heck, you're never too rich
to enjoy a free turkey dog.

00:20:58.050 --> 00:20:59.843
- Yeah, I'm starved!
- All right!

00:20:59.927 --> 00:21:01.345
- I'll take four.
- Me, too.

00:21:01.428 --> 00:21:03.263
Oh, what the hell.

00:21:10.187 --> 00:21:11.271
Here, Dwight.

00:21:11.355 --> 00:21:14.608
The boots only cost $299.99.

00:21:14.691 --> 00:21:16.652
You invest this penny like you wanted.

00:21:16.735 --> 00:21:17.736
Thanks, Dad.

00:21:17.819 --> 00:21:20.822
I'm going to take this and buy
five shares of Amazon.com.

00:21:20.906 --> 00:21:22.115
A risk-taker!

00:21:22.199 --> 00:21:23.659
That's my boy.

00:21:24.326 --> 00:21:26.453
The entire surplus is gone!

00:21:26.537 --> 00:21:28.872
Oh, what a McGovern I've been.

00:21:28.956 --> 00:21:31.875
Why did I have to issue
that crooked tax rebate?

00:21:31.959 --> 00:21:35.712
Uh, at least we got a few mildly
interesting stories out of it.

00:21:35.921 --> 00:21:37.548
Oh, my, yes.

00:21:37.714 --> 00:21:39.883
Speaking of which,
my story kind of petered out

00:21:39.967 --> 00:21:41.301
without me learning a lesson.

00:21:41.385 --> 00:21:43.512
There he is!

00:21:45.764 --> 00:21:48.016
All right! Closure!

00:21:57.442 --> 00:21:59.653
"Futurama." Noun.

00:21:59.903 --> 00:22:02.614
Um, I don't know,
you just watched it, dummy.

00:22:02.781 --> 00:22:04.283
What are you asking me for?

00:22:04.783 --> 00:22:07.786
Hey, here's a fun definition, "Idiot."

00:22:08.453 --> 00:22:09.830
Noun.

00:22:10.330 --> 00:22:11.415
You!

00:22:14.293 --> 00:22:16.920
This has been Roseanne,
your guide to the world of facts.